{
  "id": "u10-l06",
  "unit": "u10-culture",
  "title": "Invitations & guests",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "Bengali invitations use the **future** as a gentle request: **আমাদের বাসায় আসবেন** is literally 'You will come to our home', and it means 'Please do come!' More formally: **আপনাকে দাওয়াত দিলাম** 'I'm inviting you' (lit. 'I gave you an invitation'). To a friend: **তুমি কি আসবে?** 'Will you come?'\n\nSoften it with **যদি** 'if' + the present: **যদি সময় হয়, আমাদের বাসায় আসবেন** 'If you have time, please come'.\n\nA **মেহমান** (guest) is treated with great honour. Expect tea, sweets and **পিঠা** (rice cakes), and expect **খাবেন?** 'Will you have some?' more than once. A first 'no' is often heard as politeness, so accept a little.\n\n**Kolkata:** **নেমন্তন্ন** 'invitation', **অতিথি** 'guest'.",
  "vocab": [
